    <briefdescription>
<para>Updated array is divided into array items. </para>    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Each item is a range of fields. Item updates first field of the range and stores size of others to save them with no changes into a new tuple later. It allows on update of a single field in an array store at most 2 objects - item for the previous fields, and item for this one + its tail. This is how rope data structure works - a binary tree designed for big contiguous object updates. </para>    </detaileddescription>
